  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "**DI014 wrapped-result disposal precision**: DI014 now treats root providers assigned or returned through parenthesized, provable upcast, or null-forgiving `BuildServiceProvider()` results as disposed or caller-owned when appropriate — including combinations with conditional-access creations such as `(services?.BuildServiceProvider())!`. Flows that pass the result through a user-defined conversion (explicit *or* implicit operator) or an unproven downcast (`(Wrapper)(object)...`, downcast from an interface) still report, because they are not proven to hand the root provider itself to the disposal or return site.",
